      "content": "Let me read the original test file first.Now let me check the working directory and compile script to understand the setup.Now I understand the test. It verifies that evaluating a default `Gaussian` at a very large value (12^12) returns approximately 0. Let me write an improved version with better understandability.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file renames `test1()` to `testGaussianValueAtLargeInputApproachesZero()`, uses descriptive variable names (`gaussian`, `constantTwelve`, `largeInput`, `result`), and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the mathematical intent — all without changing the method calls, arguments, or assertions."
